  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Calm Band",
    "overview": "The page is a stack of full-width colour bands that alternate between off-white paper, bay-dusk navy and a deeper navy at night. Each band carries one idea, set large in Cal Sans with plenty of room around it, and a single warm dusk-amber tells the eye where to press. The world is built for a homeowner over 40 reading on a phone: 18px body at 1.6, 56px tap targets, high-contrast ink, and a page that holds still.\n\nDensity is low and the order is fixed: say who and where, prove the license, show the windows, ask for the estimate, give the number. Surfaces are flat colour; depth comes from the band change and from white cards sitting on paper, never from shadows (the one exception is the floating text circle, which has to sit above content). There are no photographs in this system; drawn line icons (2.2 to 2.6px strokes, round caps) in navy carry the imagery.\n\nMotion exists in code (a letter bounce-in for the H1, a 12px fade-up below the fold) but ships switched off (`CONFIG.MOTION = false`). The resting state is the design.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Full-bleed bands: paper, navy, deep navy with a faint diagonal line texture.",
      "One warm accent, dusk amber, used as a fill; text on it is always deep ink.",
      "Cal Sans at weight 400 for every heading, button, label and number; system sans for reading.",
      "Soft, large radii: 24px cards, 20px rows, pill buttons and chips.",
      "Still by default; every hover is a colour change only."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Amber Is a Fill Rule",
        "body": "Amber appears as a solid shape (button, disc, dot, circle) with deep ink on top. On paper, amber text switches to burnt amber ink; bright amber text is allowed only on navy grounds.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Focus Colours Rule",
        "body": "On light bands focus is a 3px navy outline at 3px offset; on navy and night bands it switches to amber. Focus never uses the same colour as the fill it surrounds.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Display Does the Talking Rule",
        "body": "Anything a visitor taps or scans (buttons, labels, rows, phone numbers) is set in Cal Sans; only prose and form input use the system face.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Phone Number Rule",
        "body": "Phone numbers are Cal Sans with tabular figures, word-spacing -0.15em, never wrapping inside the number.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Lift Hover Rule",
        "body": "Hover never adds a shadow or moves an element. It changes a colour: a row's arrow disc turns amber, a field border turns navy, amber lightens.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep body copy at 18px/1.6 and every tap target at least 44px (buttons and fields 56px).",
      "**Do** alternate bands paper, navy, night; put the line texture only on navy-family grounds.",
      "**Do** put deep ink on amber, and switch amber text to burnt amber ink on paper.",
      "**Do** set headings, buttons, labels and phone numbers in Cal Sans 400.",
      "**Do** ship still: motion stays behind `CONFIG.MOTION` and off for this audience."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use amber as body or label text on light grounds.",
      "**Don't** add shadows to cards, rows or buttons; the floating circle is the only lifted element.",
      "**Don't** make hover move, lift or glow anything.",
      "**Don't** add a sticky bottom call bar; the single floating circle is the persistent action.",
      "**Don't** add eyebrow labels above headings on new surfaces; the three pills on index.html are carried by the build, not a pattern to extend.",
      "**Don't** use Cal Sans bold or a second display face; the system has one display weight."
